'''Taguig–Pateros's 1st congressional district''' is one of the two [[congressional districts of the Philippines]] in the combined independent local government units of [[Pateros, Metro Manila|Pateros]] and [[Taguig]]. It has been represented in the [[House of Representatives of the Philippines]] since 2007.<ref name="congleg">{{cite web|url=http://www.congress.gov.ph/legislators/?v=province |title=Roster of Philippine legislators |publisher=[[House of Representatives of the Philippines]] |accessdate=February 10, 2021}}</ref> The district was created in 2004 following a plebiscite to ratify Republic Act No. 8487 or the 1998 Taguig City Charter.<ref name="apportion">{{cite web|url=http://lawyerly.ph/laws/view/l1201 |title=Republic Act No. 8487 |publisher=Lawyerly |accessdate=February 10, 2021}}</ref> It consists of the entire [[Municipalities of the Philippines|municipality]] of Pateros and the eastern Taguig [[barangay]]s of [[Bagumbayan, Taguig|Bagumbayan]], [[Bambang, Taguig|Bambang]], [[Calzada, Taguig|Calzada]], Comembo, Hagonoy, [[Ibayo-Tipas]], Ligid-Tipas, Lower Bicutan, [[New Lower Bicutan]], [[Napindan]], Palingon, Pembo, Rizal, San Miguel, [[Santa Ana, Taguig|Santa Ana]], [[Tuktukan]], [[Ususan]] and Wawa.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.rappler.com/philippines/elections/comelec-allows-embo-residents-taguig-vote-congressman-2025/|title=Comelec allows EMBO residents in Taguig to vote for congressman in 2025|date=September 27, 2024|accessdate=September 28, 2024|work=Rappler|first=Dwight|last=de Leon}}</ref> The district is currently represented in the [[20th Congress of the Philippines|20th Congress]] by Ading Cruz of the [[Nacionalista Party]] (NP).<ref name="congmem">{{cite web|url=https://www.congress.gov.ph/members/ |title=House Members |publisher=[[House of Representatives of the Philippines]] |accessdate=March 12, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Sampang |first=Dianne |date=September 23, 2024 |title=Comelec adopts Taguig ordinance on Embo barangays|url=https://newsinfo.inquirer.net/1987391/comelec-adopts-taguig-ordinance-on-embo-barangays |access-date=September 27, 2024 |publisher=Philippine Daily Inquirer |language=en}}</ref>
